WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.600
Ready to leave the vault?&nbsp;
Amazon's new Fallout series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.120
is nearly here — and the first trailer&nbsp;
is packed full of fan-friendly details.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.480
Amazon Studios has dropped the first teaser&nbsp;
trailer for its Fallout series. This iconic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.320
post-apocalyptic RPG series continues to be&nbsp;
one of the most popular video game franchises&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.960
of all time. Although the series debuted&nbsp;
in 1997, it was 2008's highly immersive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.600
Fallout 3 that turned the series into a&nbsp;
must-play for gamers. For the uninitiated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.560
players take on the role of an individual&nbsp;
living in a vault made to withstand nuclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.800
fallout. Through various circumstances,&nbsp;
they're forced out of their comfort zone and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.560
enter an apocalyptic hellscape, confronting&nbsp;
devious humans and terrifying creatures.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.120
The Fallout television adaptation, which comes&nbsp;
from Westworld creatives Lisa Joy and Jonathan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.360
Nolan, will be an original story that's canonical&nbsp;
to the video games. Based purely on the first look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:54.960
of the series, hardcore fans will be pleased with&nbsp;
the show's direction. The teaser trailer is ripe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.160
with imagery and iconography that's ripped&nbsp;
directly from the video game, such as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.760
iconic look of the vaults and post-apocalyptic&nbsp;
Earth's many dastardly creatures. There are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:12.200
however, some small but important details that&nbsp;
fans might have missed in this first trailer.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.920
"I grabbed a mouldy one."

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:17.040
While the Fallout games take place&nbsp;
in the same universe and timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.560
they're not necessarily interconnected&nbsp;
like traditional sequels. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.440
the games feature similar themes, mechanics, and&nbsp;
— sometimes — characters. Perhaps one of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.680
interesting "characters" in the franchise is&nbsp;
Dogmeat, a dog who serves as a companion for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:34.040
the playable character. Dogmeat has become a&nbsp;
prominent part of the Fallout lore, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.280
why it shouldn't be surprising that he's set to&nbsp;
make an appearance in the Amazon's adaptation.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.480
And it seems like Dogmeat is making more than&nbsp;
just a cameo appearance in the Fallout series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.560
as he appears a number of times throughout&nbsp;
the trailer. Featuring Dogmeat in the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.160
directly ties the show to the video games,&nbsp;
making his appearance a truly fun piece of fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.040
service. And seeing as there's a different&nbsp;
Dogmeat in each game, the creatives have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.240
carte blanche to create a version of the dog&nbsp;
that perfectly suits the television series.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.640
Meanwhile, in the Fallout lore, there are over&nbsp;
100 vaults — though not all of them have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.000
explored in the games. With the release of the&nbsp;
television series, fans are on track to see a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.200
brand-new vault that hasn't appeared before.&nbsp;
In the trailer, audiences see the protagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.480
Lucy, leave Vault 33 and set off for the&nbsp;
outside world for reasons as yet unknown.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.280
Little is known about Vault&nbsp;
33, which is what makes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.280
all the more intriguing. The vault is&nbsp;
located in what was once Los Angeles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.480
which makes sense considering vaults with low&nbsp;
numbers were built for the West Coast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.320
it looks like something devious is being cooked&nbsp;
up at Vault 33. When we see Lucy step out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:38.760
Vault 33 for the first time, a cut can be seen&nbsp;
on her lip. Did she get into a fight? If so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.880
with whom? Another moment appears to depict total&nbsp;
bedlam happening in a vault — though whether it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.160
Vault 33 isn't yet known. The Fallout series isn't&nbsp;
shying away from showing that things are imperfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:54.280
in both the sheltered and outside world, and it&nbsp;
seems that the series will carry on this theme.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:03:00.400
Notably, Fallout will be set in the year 2296&nbsp;
— about 200 years after the apocalypse. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.480
year in which the show is set is important as&nbsp;
it helps inform fans of when the show takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.200
place in the larger Fallout timeline.&nbsp;
The franchise's last mainline entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:14.040
Fallout 4, is set in 2287, which means the&nbsp;
television series begins after all the games.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.760
Still, the show features components seen&nbsp;
throughout the franchise. These include the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.000
Power Armors, a key aspect of the franchise in&nbsp;
terms of gameplay and visual recognition. Fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.200
will also spot the military group Brotherhood&nbsp;
of Steel; their symbol can be seen on the Power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.360
Armors. Another key piece of iconography&nbsp;
ripped from the games is the Vertibird&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.160
flying vehicle. First introduced in Fallout 2,&nbsp;
the vehicles are seen briefly in the trailer.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.280
Based purely on the trailer, Fallout seems like&nbsp;
it'll be an authentic adaptation that honors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:45.200
its source material while offering a unique&nbsp;
story. And while fans no doubt have questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:51.201
about the series, all will be answered when&nbsp;
Fallout hits Prime Video on April 12th, 2024.

